3. RTKLIB (BSD 2-clause License)
--------------------------------

Where and what (all in the gnx_py package):

  gnx_py/models/ocean_loading.py, the table _OTL_ARGS and the function
        otl_arguments: a Python port of the ocean tide loading displacement of
        RTKLIB 2.4.2 p13, src/ppp.c, function tide_oload (Copyright (C)
        2010-2018 by T.TAKASU, All rights reserved): its args[][5] table
        (angular speed and Doodson multipliers of the 11 BLQ constituents) is
        copied value for value, and the astronomical arguments repeat its
        arithmetic and summation order. RTKLIB took the arguments from the IERS
        routine ARG.f (Doodson angles h0, s0, p0 at 0h UT); ocean_loading_enu
        rotates the result as RTKLIB's tidedisp does.

  gnx_py/models/corrections.py, the functions windupcorr and
        process_windup_correction_vectorized: the phase wind-up of RTKLIB 2.4.2,
        src/rtkcmn.c, function windupcorr (T. Takasu; model of Wu et al., 1993),
        ported with its vectors and arithmetic; the vectorised function repeats
        it over epochs (unwrapped with numpy.unwrap) and optionally takes the
        satellite body axes of an attitude model or the orbit-normal frame.

  gnx_py/ppp/pppar.py, the functions ldldecom, decorrel and ssearch (with the
        helpers _gauss, _perm, _round_half_up and _sgn): a Python port of the
        LAMBDA / MLAMBDA integer least-squares estimation of RTKLIB 2.4.2,
        src/lambda.c (functions LD, gauss, perm, reduction and search; T. Takasu).
        The differences are described in the source.

RTKLIB itself is not part of this repository. Apart from the files listed above,
the GNX docstrings and comments that name an RTKLIB function (for example the mean
pole and pole tide of gnx_py/models/tides.py, which follow the IERS Conventions
2010 equations as RTKLIB tide_pole and iers_mean_pole do) describe the model GNX
follows and are a reference, not a copy of RTKLIB code.

